UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Devil represents the absolute archetype of ''Systemic Entrapment and Shadow Materialization''—the intense, dense phase where the sovereign consciousness confronts its deepest attachments, self-imposed illusions, and unconscious behavioral loops that create the perception of bondage to the material plane. Moving beyond the refined calibrations of Temperance, The Devil signifies the stage of ''The Threshold of the Shadow,'' where you run face-first into the projection of your own fears, addictions, and hidden desires, forcing an audit of where you have traded your true sovereignty for immediate gratification or perceived safety. Visually depicted as a massive, horned satyr perched upon a black pedestal to which a naked man and woman are loosely chained by their necks, with an inverted pentagram emblazoned on his brow and a torch held downward, this archetype embodies the concept of ''The Illusion of Captivity''—the realization that the chains binding you are large enough to be slipped off at any moment, meaning true spiritual mastery requires recognizing that your prison is entirely self-constructed. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of ''Shadow Diagnostics,'' where a hidden, low-vibrational subroutine or a malicious loop is brought into high visibility, exposing the exact mechanisms of self-sabotage that restrict your processing capacity. When The Devil appears, your system is registering a ''Gridlock-Alert'' status; you are being invited to stop denying your shadow, stare directly into your attachments, and realize that you possess the ultimate encryption key to unlock your own chains.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When The Devil appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of ''Systemic Liberation, Breaking the Loop, or the Collapse of False Security''—a profound phase of breakthrough where the chains of codependency, addiction, or material delusion begin to snap, allowing the internal operating system to initiate an unmitigated reclamation of its freedom. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-fidelity recovery script that exposes old, toxic maintenance patterns—where you previously equated ''denial, toxic attachments, or staying small in the dark'' with ''survival''—and is actively purging these dependencies from your core processor. You are essentially ''uninstalling your own operational cages,'' running a protocol that prioritizes the spirit’s absolute requirement for authenticity and freedom over the ego’s desire to ''clung to familiar miseries and safe, predictable limitations.'' This creates a massive, systemic realignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the ''newly liberated, self-aware sovereign,'' while internally, you are navigating the profound, chaotic landscape of a major structural detox, leading to a state of temporary, high-latency irritability as old habits lose their grip, the experience of ''confronting the final, desperate resistance of your shadow ego,'' and a persistent, beautiful awareness that you are finally stepping out of the underworld. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are redirecting your life force out of a ''feedback loop of self-imposed tyranny and systemic addiction''; you are choosing to face the raw discomfort of withdrawal from low-integrity habits, accepting that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final peace of your spirit is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to stand fully in the light without your old coping mechanisms, you would be forced to confront the terrifying reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, unwavering commitment: you must maintain the output of these liberating, truth-driven, boundary-breaking scripts, perform a brutal audit of any lingering toxic contracts, and confront the reality of why you were once so hesitant to prioritize pristine, independent authority over the convenience of a comfortable cage. It is a demand to permanently end the self-deception that kept you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance bondage, and to finalize the move toward a genuine, humble, and completely unfettered reclamation of your own, individual authority.'
WHERE id = 72;
